    'process' => [['Split the goals', 'B2B pipeline vs local demand defined separately.'], ['Build and track', 'Accounts, pixels and forms live before budget.'], ['Test creative', 'Hooks and offers rotated on a fixed cadence.'], ['Scale winners', 'Budget follows qualified cost per lead.']],
    'measure' => ['Cost per qualified lead by platform', 'Lead-to-opportunity rate', 'CTR and hook-rate on TikTok', 'LinkedIn form completion rate', 'Creative test velocity'],
    'fit' => 'LinkedIn suits professional, financial, legal and B2B suppliers. TikTok suits visual trades, clinics, consumer services and employer branding. Many clients run both with different offers.',
    'related' => ['meta-ads', 'ai-ads-optimisation', 'video-production'],
    'faqs' => [['Do I need both platforms?', 'Only if audiences and offers justify both. We will recommend one starter platform when budget is tight.'], ['Can you use my employee advocates?', 'Yes, with clear guidelines. Employee posts often outperform polished brand creative on both platforms.'], ['Are LinkedIn lead forms any good?', 'They convert well; quality depends on questions and follow-up speed. We design forms to pre-qualify.'], ['Do TikTok ads need influencers?', 'Not required. Spark Ads with creators help, but strong organic-style creative from your team can work.'], ['Who owns the ad accounts?', 'You do. We work inside accounts in your business name.'], ['What budgets make sense?', 'LinkedIn CPCs are high — budgets must match deal values. TikTok can test lower. We model before launch.'],
